# winoracle 2026-09-28, WARP, FL 11_1, x64 (x86 identical). Vitreo verdicts:
#  O1 every blend factor (colour + alpha), dual source SRC1_*, BlendFactor,
#     RGBA32F exact and RGBA8 within 1 LSB: CORRECT
#  O1 SRC_COLOR as an alpha factor: Windows E_INVALIDARG, Vitreo accepts (area 04)
#  O2 all five blend ops, MIN/MAX ignore factors, UNORM clamps: CORRECT (<=1 LSB)
#  O3 out-of-range blend factor / source clamping per format: CORRECT
#  O4 IndependentBlendEnable, per-target masks: CORRECT; O5 write masks: CORRECT
#  O6 logic ops: Vitreo FL 11_0, OutputMergerLogicOp=0, CreateBlendState1
#     refuses -> consistent (optional below 11_1)
#  O7 SampleMask: WRONG (ignored on 4x and 1x targets)
#  O8 AlphaToCoverageEnable: WRONG (ignored, 4x and 1x)
#  O9 sRGB blending: CORRECT. Blending enabled on R32_UINT: WRONG -- the
#     host process aborts (Metal validation: R32Uint not blendable);
#     Windows ignores BlendEnable on integer targets. Printed last.
